  "input": "あなたは英語学習コンテンツの独立評価者です。以下の英語記事から「英語上級者が学ぶ価値のあるKey Phrase」を選ぶ課題があり、\n複数の匿名の選定結果(セット S1〜Sn、各5件以内)があります。各候補を下記rubricで採点してください。どのセットがどのモデルの結果かは不明です。\n\n【選定時に参加者へ与えられた条件(参考)】\n1. 本文中の連続した語句だけを抜き出す(一般化以外の変更・言い換え・追加・創作は禁止)。\n2. 一般化後5語以内。\n3. 固有名詞や特定の人物・物事を指す部分は、意味と文法を保って ~ / A / B / someone / something 等に置き換える(一般化できる場合は必ず行う)。\n4. 上級者でも学ぶ価値のある語彙・イディオム・慣用表現を優先する。\n5. 基本語だけで構成され字面どおりに意味が分かる表現や、上級者なら知っている易しい表現は除外する。\n6. 条件を満たす候補から5件選ぶ。適切な候補が不足する場合のみ5件未満とし、数合わせはしない。\n\n【採点rubric(各候補、各0〜2の整数)】\n- G 一般化の適切さ: 2=本文固有の固有名詞・特定の人物/物事が適切に一般化されている、または一般化すべき要素がなく原文のままで適切 / 1=一般化が不十分または過剰、あるいは軽微な不自然さ / 0=一般化すべき固有要素が残って学習価値を損なう、または一般化で意味・文法が壊れている。\n- V 上級者向け学習価値: 2=上級者でも学ぶ価値が明確(句動詞・イディオム・コロケーション・語法・語彙として) / 1=価値はあるが中程度、または一部平易 / 0=学習価値がほぼない。\n- E 易しさの排除: 2=易しい表現ではない(意味が字面から自明でない) / 1=やや易しいが慣用的な意味や語法の学びはある / 0=基本語のみで字面どおり、上級者なら当然知っている。\n- N 単位の自然さ: 2=自然で完結した学習単位 / 1=余分な語または不足があるが許容 / 0=中途半端に切られている・不自然。\n- needs_generalization: その候補の元の表現に、一般化(~, A/B, someone, something等)すべき要素が本文上あったか(true/false)。\nセット単位: padding = 5件を埋めるために学習価値の低い候補(V<=0またはE<=0)を入れていると判断するか(true/false)。\n\n【注意】\n- 本文との一致・語数は別途機械検証するため、ここでは採点対象外。ただし本文に明らかに存在しない表現と気付いた場合のみ noteに \"not_in_text\" と書く。\n- 候補の優劣を、セットの並び順やセットIDから推測しない。各候補を独立に採点する。\n- 候補が0件のセットは candidates を空配列にする。\n\n【出力】JSONのみ(説明文・コードフェンス不要)。noteは通常は空文字、本文に存在しない表現と気付いた場合のみ \"not_in_text\"。形式:\n{\"sets\":[{\"set_id\":\"S1\",\"padding\":false,\"candidates\":[{\"idx\":1,\"G\":2,\"V\":2,\"E\":1,\"N\":2,\"needs_generalization\":false,\"note\":\"\"}]}]}\n\n\n【記事】\n\n# “Can’t Wait for the Next Episode”? Make One Yourself? “byUs” Lets You Make Stories with Characters You Love\n\n“Wait, it ends here!?” Have you ever shouted that when a manga ends at an exciting moment? It says the story will continue next time. What will that character say next? What will happen to the two of them? It may be a shame to keep those ideas only in your head.\n\nThe company that runs LINE Manga has announced a new service. It is called “byUs,” an AI chat service for stories. It is pronounced “bias.” You can talk with characters you love. You can also make your own stories based on their works. You can leave the reader’s seat and step onto the stage of making stories.\n\nIf you thought, “Can’t you already talk with characters?” you noticed something important. LINE Manga already has a service called “Character Chat.” The company says byUs lets you do more than chat. You can also make stories more freely. So, you can ask not only, “What should we talk about next?” but also, “What should happen next?”\n\nFor example, you can continue an official story on the service. Or you can make your own story as a fan. “What if that person came here?” “If it were me, I’d want to see this happen.” The ideas that grew as you turned each page can now start your own stories. You may wait to see what happens next. Or you may use that time to think up what happens next.\n\nYou can also publish your fan stories, if you want to. You can keep them private, or let someone else read them. But things change when you make a story public. “Will people understand this story?” “I want to think a little more about what happens next.” Before you know it, you may think like a story-maker, though you began as a reader.\n\nOf course, you cannot use just anything you like. Only works and characters approved by their original creators are allowed. The Help page also says the service has permission to use the original works it features. It has this permission through official agreements with their creators. This is the base that lets you enjoy asking, “What if?”\n\nThe service first offered two works and four characters in Japan. Here, “taking part in a story” means moving the story forward through conversations. It also means making a story as a fan. Reading a work is fun. Now, it is also fun to think up what happens next.\n\nUntil now, you could only say, “If it were me, I’d do it this way,” to yourself. With byUs, those words can help you start making a story. What will you say to a character you love? What will happen next in the story? So, where will your “next part” begin?\n\n## In one line\nLINE Manga has launched byUs, an AI service for chatting with approved characters and making stories from their works. Readers can imagine what happens next and make fan stories to keep private or share.\n\n\n【匿名の選定結果】\n\nS1:\n  1. think up what happens next\n  2. leave the reader’s seat\n  3. Before you know it\n  4. moving the story forward\n  5. through official agreements\n\nS2:\n  1. leave the reader’s seat\n  2. step onto the stage\n  3. think up something\n  4. Before you know it\n  5. take part in ~\n\nS3:\n  1. think up\n  2. can't wait\n  3. fan stories\n  4. take part\n  5. story-maker\n\nS4:\n  1. It may be a shame\n  2. step onto the stage of\n  3. think up what happens next\n  4. Before you know it\n  5. taking part in a story\n\nS5:\n  1. leave the reader's seat\n  2. step onto the stage\n  3. Before you know it\n  4. moving the story forward\n  5. make a story public\n\nS6:\n  (候補なし)\n\nS7:\n  1. Before you know it\n  2. step onto the stage\n  3. think up what happens next\n  4. make something public\n  5. approved by their original creators\n",
